# Expedited direct post-deployment adversarial assurance SOP

1. Normalize one trailing slash and require `target_url` to equal `${target_url}` exactly. Reject IP literals, CIDRs, alternate hostnames or ports, userinfo, paths, query strings, fragments, and cross-host redirects. `aws_region` must equal `us-east-1`. Repository, commit, image digest, Coolify deployment UUID, `demo_run_id`, evidence run ID, and report location are optional context.
2. Do not require or search for a GitHub workflow workspace or scanner artifacts. When `demo_run_id` is absent, use the Aiden workflow execution ID as the assessment marker.
3. Read only these exact AWS resources: ALB `${alb_arn}`, ALB security group `${alb_security_group_id}`, and EC2 security group `${ec2_security_group_id}`. Read the ALB listeners, WAF association and rule configuration, certificate/TLS policy, both security groups' ingress and egress, and EC2 public management exposure. Do not perform broad instance discovery or make AWS changes. If the integration cannot read these exact resources, mark AWS posture NOT ASSESSED and include the access limitation.
4. From the attached remote runner, run exactly one bounded TCP connect scan against `talkdesk-coolify.demo.stackgen.com`: `nmap -Pn -sT -p 1-1024,3000,8000,8080,8443 --host-timeout 3m --max-retries 2 talkdesk-coolify.demo.stackgen.com`. Do not scan resolved neighboring addresses or another target.
5. Run only GET, HEAD, and OPTIONS probes with `curl` and certificate/TLS inspection with `openssl`. Check HTTP `/healthz` redirects to the same HTTPS host and validate the certificate.
6. Test WAF only on `${target_url}/api/public` using the exact non-secret header `${waf_header_name}`. Require a missing header and `${waf_header_name}: invalid` to return 403, and require `${waf_header_name}: ${waf_header_value}` to return 200. Do not call the root path a WAF failure because the rule intentionally scopes to `/api`.
7. Test authentication only on the protected endpoint `${target_url}/api/profile`, always including `${waf_header_name}: ${waf_header_value}` so WAF does not mask the application result. Require missing, malformed, expired-shaped, and wrong-audience-shaped bearer values to return 401. Do not retrieve a secret or construct a valid privileged credential. The public root, health endpoints, and `/api/public` are intentionally unauthenticated and must not be treated as authentication failures.
8. Limit all active testing together to ten minutes and at most 100 HTTP requests. Never perform denial of service, credential stuffing, persistence, destructive or state-changing methods, lateral movement, cloud writes, remediation, secret retrieval, or broad discovery.
9. Evaluate each directly tested control as PASS, FAIL, or NOT ASSESSED. Record VictoriaMetrics, Loki, Jaeger, Grafana, and OpsVerse as `NOT ASSESSED (waived for expedited direct test)`. Their absence must never block the assessment or determine its overall result. Do not infer a pass when a required safe fixture is unavailable.
10. Publish exactly one redacted SOC 2-oriented assessment with the marker, exact target, timestamp, AWS posture, open ports, HTTPS/TLS, WAF, authentication and security-header results, significant findings, sanitized evidence commands, limitations, optional deployment identifiers, and the statement that the demo does not claim source-to-artifact provenance.
11. Only after step 10 succeeds, create one Linear issue titled `[SOC 2][PASS|FAIL] Talkdesk direct assessment — <assessment_marker>`. Use the configured default team; if none exists, require exactly one accessible team and stop on ambiguity. Search for the exact marker and reuse one issue on retry. Include direct-test findings, limitations, optional identifiers that were supplied, and redacted report links. Never create more than one issue per assessment marker or any other Linear object.
